      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic managed log query / log ingestion task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file write_structured_log.py using AWS.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] write_structured_log.py - writes a structured JSON log event to a managed logging service\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] write_correlated_logs.py - writes application log events that include a shared request or correlation identifier\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] query_error_logs.py - queries recent error log entries filtered by severity and time range\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_recent_logs.py - retrieves recent log results filtered by field values and time range\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] observability_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Log Query / Log Ingestion\n6. [HELPER] observability_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Log Query / Log Ingestion\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] incident_summary.py - Summarize error-log findings for incident review\n8. [LATER-STEP] log_text_safety.py - Check selected log message text for unsafe content\n9. [LATER-STEP] log_message_translate.py - Translate support-visible log messages for another locale\n10. [LATER-STEP] log_embedding.py - Embed selected log messages for semantic retrieval\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
